      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-30080",
      ":question/problem": "Two cars, $A$ and $B,$ are both initially at the point $O,$ and they both depart from $O$ at the same time. Car $A$ travels due east, and its distance from $O$ is given by $3t\\,\\text{ft}.$ Car $B$ travels due north, and its distance from $O$ is $2{t}^{2}\\,\\text{ft}.$ Here, $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. What is the rate of the change of the distance between the two cars after $2$ seconds?"
